00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.630 align:start position:0%
tomorrow some ccsd pre-k through third  graders return to campus for the first  time  in almost a year it's a major step for  students and families  as well as staff and tonight we're  tracking how both are preparing for the  big day  we start with reporter kristen drummond  tonight who's been speaking with  families ahead of the first day back to  class  kristin sasha some are comparing this  return to campus  as it's like the first day of school one  family in the northwest valley invited  me to see  how they're getting ready for the start  of hybrid learning  she finally gets to use her backpack  packed up and ready to go  she's got her little mouse for her  computer and then just some pencils  ari o'brien prepares for her daughter's  first day back on campus in nearly a  year i think it will be a nice change  for her  making sure she has the necessities and  a few other items  not needed in the past i gave her three  masks  and i labeled the bag clean just in case  she you know drops it how do you feel  about going  back to school tomorrow in person very  very very very 100 more  very excited addie attends gerheim  elementary school  the eight-year-old was placed in cohort  a for hybrid learning  she will attend her second grade classes  on monday and tuesday  in person then continue her studies  remotely wednesday through friday  i mean it will be nice for her to be  able to interact with the teacher  in person and see other students we're  just ready for them to get back get back  in the routine  and not be stuck at home anymore alondra  reynolds also looking forward to this  opportunity  her first grade daughter goes to hayes  elementary school the six-year-old is in  cohort b  attending class remotely monday through  wednesday and in person thursday and  friday  he's a little concerned with that  because by the time thursday and friday  hits  she's so tired from the week but  reynolds says  she welcomes this chance for some  normalcy she's excited about returning  with her  friends that's a big deal expect  elementary school students participating  in hybrid learning for at least the next  month the district plans to then  transition to full-time  in-person learning five days a week on  april 6th for pre-kindergarten  to fifth grade reporting live in the  newsroom kristen drummond 8 news now
 

